## Performance and Reliability

[QUIC (UDP)](/transport-modes#udp-quic) and [WebSockets (TCP)](/transport-modes#tcp-websockets) reach multi-gigabit throughput in loopback benchmarks. The tunnel itself is not the bottleneck.

Both transports maintain gigabit-class throughput under 2% packet loss with 25 ms delay, thanks to the high-bandwidth loopback link allowing near-instant retransmissions.

See [Benchmarks](/benchmarks) for full results.

## Interfaces

Every [entry node](/concepts) includes a built-in [CLI](/cli) and [REST API](/rest-api) for live tunnel management.

## Binary Size

Distributed as a single static binary. Use the slim build to strip out the REST API and REPL for constrained environments.

| Target | Default | Slim |
|--------|---------|------|
| Linux x64 (glibc) | 6.1 MB | 4.7 MB |
| Linux x64 (musl, static) | 6.0 MB | 4.7 MB |
| Linux arm64 | 5.4 MB | 4.1 MB |

